            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">An alert: one thing to say and nothing to decide, so one button. The handler fires on the button, not on the backdrop — a dialog that closes when the pointer slips is a dialog that loses what it was asking.  `opts`: {"ok": "Got it"}</p>
        </div>
<div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
